<title>NETHERLANDS: Nedlloyd posts NLG 37 mln Q3 net profit.</title>
<headline>Nedlloyd posts NLG 37 mln Q3 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Total net profit		    37     vs   53</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     1.63  vs    2.35</p>
<p>    Net from ordinary operations    38     vs   63</p>
<p>    Ditto per share (guilders)	 1.63  vs    2.84</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges	    nil     vs   11</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  1.73  vs    1.72</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast that transport and shipping group Koninklijke Nedlloyd Groep NV would post a Q3 net profit from ordinary operations of 20-38 million guilders  </p>
<p>    Operating profit		    40     vs   63</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    24     vs   35</p>
<p>    Interest charges		    23     vs   32</p>
<p>    Tax					3     vs    3</p>
<p>    Minority interests	   debit 1     vs    1 credit</p>
<p>NOTES - Nedlloyd noted that net profit from ordinary operations for the third quarter of 1996 included two million guilders in capital gains on assets sold.</p>
<p>Ordinary net profit for the third quarter of 1995 included 44 million guilders in capital gains on assets sold.</p>
<p>If these gains were stripped out, then net profit from ordinary operations would show a rise to 36 million guilders from 19 million in the third quarter of 1995, it said.  </p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
